      "message": "According to the diagram https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2279.txt , the only bytes that start with \"0\" are found in single-byte unicode encodings. According to http://www.fileformat.info/info/charset/UTF-8/list.htm , the unicode value of \"\\n\" is \"0a\", whose first bit is 0.\n\nSo it seems to me that this will work correctly at the cost of being somewhat confusing.\n\nI tried a bufio.Scanner as a result of your comment here, and found that it limited token sizes to 64 * 1024 bits.\nFor now I\u0027ll just extract the readline logic into a method and put a comment on it.\n\nThe json encoding does escape newlines inside of paths.",
      "parentUuid": "511d6ac6_e3860603",
      "revId": "a4f894272111427dce4bfbae0c1a9618781d2632",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
